# own-product-signin-audit.mjs — deviations TOLERATED today, per own product.
#
#   <app> <provider-id>[,<provider-id>...]    # why, and what ends it
#
# A RATCHET: rows may only be removed. A new provider on any own product fails
# the build, and a row whose provider is gone also fails until it is deleted.
# Rule: fleet STACK.md, "Auth — who the user is": own products federate to
# OrangeCat and keep no sign-in of their own.

# Recorded 2026-09-24 from each product's live /api/auth/providers — what is
# DEPLOYED, not what a branch says. Remove a provider, then delete its id here.
loki            email-password,github,google,local,user-password,x-1a   # GitHub is ALSO a connected account (repo tokens) — keep it as a link after OrangeCat sign-in, drop it as a way in
datacat         credentials
evig            credentials
petvity         credentials,google
surf-your-life  credentials,google
